# Normalise line endings in the repository so a build is a function of the
# git objects, not of whoever checked the tree out.
#
# MEASURED (candidate a6bcdd0, TT-R6-WHEEL-NONREPRODUCIBLE-001): with
# core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes, a Windows checkout rewrote every
# text file to CRLF, so two builds of the same commit shipped different bytes
# for 7 wheel members. The git objects were already LF-clean, so the only fix
# is to stop the checkout from rewriting them.
#
# This repo ships no .cmd/.bat/.ps1/.sh files (verified: `git ls-files`), so
# requiring LF for every text type cannot break a Windows-only script.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.ndjson text eol=lf
*.sha256 text eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.whl  binary
*.gz   binary
